{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "A Wildcard Hero rolls an ability on even levels, a talent on odd ones, and rerolls with a Scroll of Fortune",
  "contract": "On Darkmoon - Season 10 Wildcard the Hero's essence budget (CharacterAdvancementEssence.dbc, wildcard rows of class 10) opened an ability roll (2 AE) on every even level from 10 and a talent roll (1 TE) on every odd level from 11. The dice sent CMSG 0x643; the server revealed one entry from the pool of its wildcard level (SMSG 0x621), learned it, sent the build (SMSG 0x726) and answered ROLL_ABILITIES_OK (SMSG 0x644), or ROLL_ABILITIES_NO_ROLL without unspent essence. Talents came with a random number of ranks. A right-click on a stack of Scroll of Fortune items redeemed the whole stack into tokens (SMSG 0x670); rerolling an entry (CMSG 0x61D) spent one, unlearned the entry and answered CA_UNLEARN_OK (SMSG 0x61E), after which the client asked for the replacement roll. The client offers the starting choice whenever its build holds at most four abilities, so a reroll that leaves four abilities shows the swap only with the replacement build. Without a scroll the answer was CA_UNLEARN_NO_SCROLL_OF_FORTUNE, and an entry could not be rerolled while a roll of its kind was still unspent. The fifth spell ended the starting phase: the server emptied and unblocked the four starter skill card slots (SMSG 0x625) that had shown the starting abilities.",
  "timeout_ms": 90000,
  "players": [
    {"id": "wild", "race": 1, "class": 10, "level": 1},
    {"id": "plain", "race": 1, "class": 10, "level": 10}
  ],
  "steps": [
